; Regression test for issue #3243: a transaction that matched through a
; Payee tag votes for the account only with the postings carrying it.
;
; lookup_probable_account() matches the Payee tags of a transaction's
; postings as well as its payee, but when ranking accounts it counted
; every posting of a matching transaction, the first weighing the most.
; So `convert --auto-match` filed a "Starbucks" line under Expenses:Fuel,
; the first posting of a card statement whose Expenses:Coffee posting is
; the one tagged "Payee: Starbucks".  Only the tagged posting now votes.

2026/06/01 Card Statement
    Expenses:Fuel                          40.00 USD  ; Payee: Shell
    Expenses:Coffee                         5.00 USD  ; Payee: Starbucks
    Liabilities:CC

test --auto-match --account Liabilities:CC convert $sourcepath/test/input/3243_tag.csv
2026/07/01 * Starbucks
    Expenses:Coffee                            -4.75
    Liabilities:CC

2026/07/02 * Shell
    Expenses:Fuel                                -38
    Liabilities:CC
end test
